<title>FRANCE: MATIF commodities volume rose in September.</title>
<headline>MATIF commodities volume rose in September.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of comodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange in September rose 56.3 percent from the previous month but fell 4.3 percent from September 1995, MATIF said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for commodity contracts were as follows.</p>
<p>		     Volume    Change    Change    Open Positions</p>
<p>				   on month  on year   at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts    28,846     56.3     -4.3	14,532</p>
<p> Total futures    28,446     54.7     -5.6	14,182</p>
<p>Of which -</p>
<p> White sugar ($)  22,102     75.1    -13.2	 8,201</p>
<p> Potatoes		307    -77.6     83.7	   791</p>
<p> Rapeseed	    4,813     39.9     72.8	 4,510</p>
<p> Wheat		 1,224     28.2	NA	    680</p>
<p> Sugar options	 400    471.4	NA	    350</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
